@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+Feature: DOM stability across state changes
+  As a user interacting with my todo list
+  I want the app to preserve existing DOM nodes when toggling items
+  So that external tools and browser automation can maintain element references
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggling a todo preserves its DOM node
+
+    Scenario: Toggling a todo checkbox does not replace its list item node
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo item "Buy milk" has the class "completed"
+
+    Scenario: Un-toggling a completed todo checkbox does not replace its list item node
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo item "Buy milk" does not have the class "completed"
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all preserves all list item nodes
+
+    Scenario: Checking toggle-all does not replace list item nodes
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user checks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      And the todo "Buy eggs" is completed
+
+    Scenario: Unchecking toggle-all does not replace list item nodes
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user unchecks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not completed
+      And the todo "Buy eggs" is not completed
